Encrypted PDF files for the tests (Test/Tests/Encryption.hs)

source.pdf is the output of source.hs (HPDF): one page with the text
"Encrypted text", and the author "HPDF fixture" in the trailer.
source-metadata.pdf is the same document with a metadata stream
("Metadata in clear text").

qpdf 12.4.2 encrypted it with the user password "user" and the owner
password "owner" (make-fixtures.sh), into one file for each revision of the
standard security handler:

  r2-rc4-40.pdf              /R 2, RC4 40 bits
  r3-rc4-128.pdf             /R 3, RC4 128 bits
  r3-rc4-128-empty-user.pdf  /R 3, RC4 128 bits, an empty user password
  r4-rc4-128.pdf             /R 4, RC4 128 bits (crypt filter /V2)
  r4-aes-128.pdf             /R 4, AES-128 (/AESV2), with object streams
  r5-aes-256.pdf             /R 5, AES-256 (Adobe extension level 3)
  r6-aes-256.pdf             /R 6, AES-256 (PDF 2.0), with object streams

and, from source-metadata.pdf, with /EncryptMetadata false (the metadata
stream is not encrypted; for /R 4 this changes the key of the file):

  r4-aes-128-clear-metadata.pdf  /R 4, AES-128
  r6-aes-256-clear-metadata.pdf  /R 6, AES-256

and:

  r3-rc4-128-metadata.pdf        /R 3, from source-metadata.pdf
  r3-rc4-128-pdfdoc.pdf          /R 3, the passwords "l’été" (user) and
                                 "5€" (owner), in PDFDocEncoding
  r3-rc4-128-restricted.pdf      /R 3, no permission except accessibility
  r6-aes-256-restricted.pdf      /R 6, the same permissions
  r6-aes-256-empty-user-restricted.pdf
                                 /R 6, an empty user password, and the
                                 permission to print (low quality)
  r6-aes-256-same-passwords.pdf  /R 6, "same" is the user password and
                                 the owner password

The incremental updates (Test/Tests/Update.hs) also use:

  objstm.pdf                     not encrypted, with object streams and a
                                 cross-reference stream

qpdf is an implementation of the handler that is independent of HPDF. To
make the files again, in this directory:

  docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/w -w /w debian:sid sh make-fixtures.sh
